1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--learning-words-with-anki","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/learning-words-with-anki","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/learning-words-with-anki","sourceHash":"d587c164002fc12fbd9fd1c42ec509a72fce07b65dec76fbf731cae6e77ead41","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T16:53:16.401Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Learning words with Anki","zh":"使用 Anki 学习单词"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Vocabulary is the foundation of language learning. To reach fluency, you'll need to learn thousands of words. And one of the most popular tools for doing this is Anki — a spaced repetition system (SRS) that shows you flashcards at increasing intervals, right before you're likely to forget them. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/vocabulary-size\">Vocabulary Size</a>","zh":"词汇是语言学习的基础。要达到流利程度，你需要学习数千个单词。Anki 是最受欢迎的学习工具之一——它是一套间隔重复系统（SRS），会逐渐拉长闪卡的出现间隔，并在你可能遗忘之前及时展示卡片。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/vocabulary-size\">词汇量</a>"}},{"id":"what-is-anki","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What Is Anki?","zh":"Anki 是什么？"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Anki is a flashcard app that uses a spaced repetition algorithm. You study cards, tell the app whether you remembered them, and it schedules your next review. Cards you know well get shown less often. Cards you struggle with come up more frequently.","zh":"Anki 是一款采用间隔重复算法的闪卡应用。你学习卡片，告诉应用自己是否记住了内容，它便会安排下一次复习。熟悉的卡片出现频率会降低，难以记住的卡片则会更频繁地出现。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You can think of Anki like an Instant Pot in your kitchen — it's a specific, fairly niche tool that lets you do a lot more than you could without it. But you still need ingredients, a recipe, and your own effort to actually cook something. Just owning an Instant Pot won't make you a chef, and just having Anki won't make you fluent.","zh":"你可以把 Anki 想象成厨房里的电压力锅——它是一种功能明确、用途相对专门的工具，能让你完成许多没有它就很难完成的事。但要真正做出一道菜，你仍然需要食材、食谱和自己的努力。仅仅拥有电压力锅不会让你成为厨师，仅仅拥有 Anki 也不会让你的语言变得流利。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Anki is popular specifically because it's just the framework. You fill it with what you want to learn. There are thousands of pre-made decks available, or you can create your own cards from your immersion (which is called sentence mining). <a href=\"/roadmap/library/sentence-mining\">Sentence Mining</a>","zh":"Anki 之所以受欢迎，正是因为它只是一个框架。你可以把想学的内容填进去。你可以使用数千种现成牌组，也可以从自己的沉浸内容中制作卡片（这称为句子挖掘）。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/sentence-mining\">句子挖掘</a>"}},{"id":"what-anki-does-and-doesnt-do","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What Anki Does and Doesn't Do","zh":"Anki 能做什么，又不能做什么"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Anki is great at:</strong>","zh":"<strong>Anki 非常擅长：</strong>"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Helping you become <em>aware</em> of new words — creating that initial \"dictionary entry\" in your brain","zh":"帮助你<em>注意到</em>新词——在大脑中为它建立最初的“词典条目”"},{"en":"Giving you handholds in the language from day one, so immersion isn't a totally blank wall","zh":"从第一天起就在语言中为你提供抓手，让沉浸不再像面对一堵完全空白的墙"},{"en":"Keeping words fresh in your memory so you recognize them when they come up naturally","zh":"让单词在记忆中保持鲜活，以便它们自然出现时，你能认出它们"}]},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Anki does not:</strong>","zh":"<strong>Anki 不能：</strong>"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Teach you how a word <em>feels</em> — the subtle differences between words like \"kick\" and \"punt\"","zh":"教会你一个词带来的<em>语感</em>——例如“kick”和“punt”这类词之间的细微区别"},{"en":"Give you all the definitions and uses of a word — it usually only teaches one meaning at a time","zh":"一次教给你一个词的所有释义和用法——它通常每次只教授一个含义"},{"en":"Replace actual time with the language — memorizing a word is not the same as acquiring it","zh":"取代你真正接触这门语言的时间——记住一个词并不等于习得它"}]},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The key insight is this: Anki creates the initial dictionary entry. Your immersion fills it in. Study primes your brain to notice and learn words; immersion is where the actual acquisition happens. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">The Pillars of Language Learning</a>","zh":"关键在于：Anki 建立最初的词典条目，沉浸则为它补充完整内容。学习会让大脑做好准备，更容易注意和学习单词；真正的语言习得则发生在沉浸之中。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">语言学习的支柱</a>"}},{"id":"getting-set-up","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Getting Set Up","zh":"开始设置"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"en":"Download Anki from the official website (<a href=\"https://apps.ankiweb.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">apps.ankiweb.net</a>). It's free on desktop and Android. The iOS app is a one-time purchase which funds the entire Anki project.","zh":"从官方网站（<a href=\"https://apps.ankiweb.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">apps.ankiweb.net</a>）下载 Anki。桌面版和 Android 版免费；iOS 版为一次性付费，收入用于支持整个 Anki 项目。"},{"en":"Get a deck to study. You can find pre-made frequency decks for most languages. See \"Where to Get a Deck\" below for more info.","zh":"获取一个用于学习的牌组。大多数语言都有现成的高频词牌组。更多信息请参阅下方的“从哪里获取牌组”。"},{"en":"Import the deck by double-clicking the .apkg file, or use File → Import in Anki.","zh":"双击 .apkg 文件导入牌组，或在 Anki 中选择“文件 → 导入”。"},{"en":"Create a free AnkiWeb account and sync your data. This lets you study on multiple devices and never lose your progress.","zh":"创建免费的 AnkiWeb 账户并同步数据。这样你就能在多台设备上学习，也不必担心丢失学习进度。"}]},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If you're going to study on your phone, set things up on your computer first and then sync to your phone. It's much easier that way. On Android, the app is called AnkiDroid. On iOS, it's called Anki (not AnkiApp — that's a different thing).","zh":"如果准备在手机上学习，请先在电脑上完成设置，再同步到手机。这样会轻松得多。在 Android 上，这款应用名为 AnkiDroid；在 iOS 上则名为 Anki（不是 AnkiApp——那是另一款应用）。"}},{"id":"recommended-settings","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Recommended Settings","zh":"推荐设置"}},{"id":"segment-0016","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>New cards per day:</strong> Start with 5–10. If you're a total beginner, start with 5–7. If you've studied some of the language before, 10 is fine. This might feel slow at first, but after a couple of weeks, reviews pile up and you'll be glad you kept it manageable.","zh":"<strong>每日新卡数量：</strong>从 5～10 张开始。如果你是零基础初学者，就从 5～7 张开始；如果以前学过一些这门语言，每天 10 张也没问题。起初可能会觉得进度很慢，但几周后复习量会逐渐累积，到时你会庆幸自己把数量控制在了可承受的范围内。"}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>FSRS:</strong> Make sure FSRS is enabled in your deck settings. It's a newer study algorithm that makes your review time shorter and more efficient.","zh":"<strong>FSRS：</strong>确保已在牌组设置中启用 FSRS。这是一种较新的学习算法，可以缩短复习时间，提高复习效率。"}},{"id":"how-to-study","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"How to Study","zh":"如何学习"}},{"id":"segment-0019","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Open a deck, click \"Study Now,\" and look at the card. Try to remember what's on the back. Press the spacebar to flip it. If you got it right, hit \"Good.\" If not, hit \"Again.\"","zh":"打开一个牌组，点击“现在学习”，然后查看卡片。试着回忆卡片背面的内容，再按空格键翻面。如果答对了，就点击“良好”；如果没答对，就点击“重来”。"}},{"id":"segment-0020","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You can entirely ignore the \"Easy\" and \"Hard\" buttons (or remove them with the <a href=\"https://ankiweb.net/shared/info/876946123\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">pass/fail addon</a>). If you were to use them correctly, they can slightly improve your review time, but only if you're consistent about what \"Easy\" and \"Hard\" actually mean. It's easier for most people to ignore them.","zh":"你完全可以忽略“简单”和“困难”按钮（也可以使用<a href=\"https://ankiweb.net/shared/info/876946123\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">通过/失败插件</a>将它们移除）。如果使用得当，它们可以略微减少复习时间，但前提是你对“简单”和“困难”的含义始终采用一致标准。对大多数人来说，直接忽略它们更省事。"}},{"id":"segment-0021","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Don't overthink the buttons. You're just telling Anki what you need to practice more. \"Again\" isn't failure — it's feedback.","zh":"不要过度纠结该按哪个按钮。你只是在告诉 Anki 哪些内容需要多加练习。“重来”并不代表失败——它只是反馈。"}},{"id":"segment-0022","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Keep studying until you see the \"Congratulations\" screen. This means you've finished all your new cards and reviews for the day. This is how you prevent cards from piling up and making Anki miserable.","zh":"继续学习，直到看到“恭喜”界面。这表示你已经完成当天的所有新卡和复习任务。这样可以防止卡片越积越多，让使用 Anki 变成一种折磨。"}},{"id":"tips-for-long-term-success","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Tips for Long-Term Success","zh":"长期坚持的建议"}},{"id":"segment-0024","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Make it comfortable.</strong> Anki out of the box is pretty ugly. Take some time to make your cards look nice — adjust text size, use colors you like, make sure the audio sounds good. If you're going to use this tool for years, it should be pleasant to use.","zh":"<strong>让使用体验更舒适。</strong>Anki 的默认外观相当简陋。花点时间把卡片设计得更美观——调整字号，使用自己喜欢的颜色，并确保音频效果良好。如果你准备使用这个工具很多年，它就应该让人用起来愉快。"}},{"id":"segment-0025","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Be picky about your cards.</strong> If a card is giving you trouble, delete it or suspend it. Words aren't rare Pokémon — you're going to come across them again in your immersion. A bad card isn't your fault; it's the card's fault. Get rid of it and move on.","zh":"<strong>严格挑选卡片。</strong>如果一张卡片总让你犯难，就删除或暂停它。单词又不是稀有宝可梦——你以后还会在沉浸中遇到它们。卡片不好并不是你的错，而是卡片本身有问题。删掉它，继续前进。"}},{"id":"segment-0026","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Don't do too much.</strong> More cards per day does not mean better learning. Trying to jam 20–30 new cards per day is like trying to sprint through a marathon. It works for a few days and then you collapse. An average of 5–10 new cards per day, sustained over months, beats any short burst.","zh":"<strong>不要做得太多。</strong>每天学更多卡片并不代表学得更好。试图每天硬塞 20～30 张新卡，就像想用冲刺的速度跑完马拉松：头几天或许可行，之后就会精疲力竭。连续几个月保持平均每天 5～10 张新卡，胜过任何短期突击。"}},{"id":"segment-0027","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Find your time and place.</strong> Choose a specific time, device, and location for your daily Anki. Doing it with your morning coffee, or in the 15 minutes before work — whatever works. When 98% of your Anki happens in one place, that last 2% is easy to fill in. It becomes like brushing your teeth.","zh":"<strong>找到适合自己的时间和地点。</strong>为每天使用 Anki 选定固定的时间、设备和地点。可以在喝早晨咖啡时学习，也可以利用上班前的 15 分钟——选择适合自己的方式即可。当 98% 的 Anki 学习都在同一个地方完成时，剩下的 2% 也很容易补上。它最终会像刷牙一样自然。"}},{"id":"segment-0028","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Focus on hit rate, not streaks.</strong> A streak feels great until it breaks, and then it's devastating. Instead, track your \"hit rate\" — the percentage of days you've done Anki in the last 6 weeks. Missing one day barely affects a 90% hit rate, but it destroys a streak. The habit matters more than the number. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/habit-health\">Habit Health</a>","zh":"<strong>关注完成率，而不是连续打卡天数。</strong>连续打卡时感觉很棒，但一旦中断，就会让人备受打击。与其如此，不如记录自己的“完成率”——过去 6 周内完成 Anki 学习的天数比例。漏掉一天几乎不会影响 90% 的完成率，却会彻底中断连续记录。习惯本身比数字更重要。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/habit-health\">习惯健康度</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0029","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Balance study with immersion.</strong> Our recommendation is to spend at most 25–30% of your learning time on study (which includes Anki) and the rest on immersion. If you're struggling to remember words in Anki, the answer isn't more Anki — it's more immersion. Seeing words in real context fills in those dictionary entries and makes everything click. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">The Pillars of Language Learning</a>","zh":"<strong>平衡学习与沉浸。</strong> 我们建议，最多将 25%–30% 的学习时间用于主动学习（包括使用 Anki），其余时间用于沉浸。如果你很难记住 Anki 中的单词，解决办法不是刷更多 Anki，而是增加沉浸。通过在真实语境中反复遇到这些单词，你会逐渐充实头脑中的“词典条目”，一切也会豁然开朗。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">语言学习的支柱</a>"}},{"id":"where-to-get-a-deck","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Where to Get a Deck","zh":"从哪里获取牌组"}},{"id":"segment-0031","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"There are many free decks on <a href=\"https://ankiweb.net/shared/decks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">AnkiWeb</a>. Thousands of Anki decks other language learners have made and put out for free. Some are very good (<a href=\"https://ankiweb.net/shared/info/1196762551\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">this Japanese deck</a>, for example), but others are pretty bad or entirely broken.","zh":"<a href=\"https://ankiweb.net/shared/decks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">AnkiWeb</a> 上有许多免费牌组，其中包括其他语言学习者制作并免费分享的数千个 Anki 牌组。有些质量很好（例如<a href=\"https://ankiweb.net/shared/info/1196762551\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">这个日语牌组</a>），但也有些相当糟糕，甚至根本无法使用。"}},{"id":"segment-0032","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The rating system in AnkiWeb helps to bring the better decks to the top, but it's a very simple system and newer decks appear at the very bottom, even if they're better.","zh":"AnkiWeb 的评分系统有助于让优质牌组排在前面，但这个系统非常简单，而且新牌组即使质量更好，也会出现在列表最底部。"}},{"id":"segment-0033","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Try searching in AnkiWeb for your target language. Look for the terms \"frequency\" or \"common words\" decks, not themed vocabulary lists. Ideally with audio and around 1000 cards.","zh":"试着在 AnkiWeb 上搜索你的目标语言。请寻找名称中包含“词频”或“常用词”的牌组，而不是按主题整理的词汇表。理想情况下，牌组应带有音频，并包含大约 1000 张卡片。"}},{"id":"segment-0034","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Refold sells fundamental vocabulary decks <a href=\"https://refold.la/category/decks/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">for several languages</a>. We decided to make them since we saw several fundamental issues with the decks on AnkiWeb.","zh":"Refold 销售<a href=\"https://refold.la/category/decks/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">多种语言</a>的基础词汇牌组。我们之所以决定制作这些牌组，是因为发现 AnkiWeb 上的牌组存在几个根本性问题。"}},{"id":"segment-0035","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Our decks include high-quality audio for the words AND sentences, images, clear definitions, a nice card design... but most importantly, we hand selected the words to ensure you're only learning the most important words.","zh":"我们的牌组为单词和例句都配有高质量音频，还包含图片、清晰的释义和美观的卡片设计……但最重要的是，我们人工筛选了其中的单词，确保你只学习最重要的词汇。"}},{"id":"segment-0036","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Many free decks just put the 1000 most common words into a deck and call it done. But we think that spending a bunch of time learning \"the\" or \"his\" or even \"conversación\" (in Spanish) isn't a good use of your time.","zh":"许多免费牌组只是把最常见的 1000 个单词放进牌组，就算大功告成。但我们认为，花大量时间学习“the”“his”，甚至西班牙语中的“conversación”，并不能有效利用你的时间。"}},{"id":"segment-0037","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"There are official Refold decks for:","zh":"Refold 官方牌组涵盖以下语言："}},{"id":"segment-0038","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/es1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Spanish</a>","zh":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/es1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">西班牙语</a>"},{"en":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/jp1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Japanese</a>","zh":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/jp1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">日语</a>"},{"en":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/en1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">English</a>","zh":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/en1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">英语</a>"},{"en":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/ko1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Korean</a>","zh":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/ko1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">韩语</a>"},{"en":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/fr1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">French</a>","zh":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/fr1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">法语</a>"},{"en":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/de1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">German</a>","zh":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/de1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">德语</a>"},{"en":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/zh1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mandarin</a>","zh":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/zh1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">普通话</a>"},{"en":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/it1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Italian</a>","zh":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/it1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">意大利语</a>"},{"en":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/cs1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Czech</a>","zh":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/cs1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">捷克语</a>"},{"en":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/sv1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Swedish</a>","zh":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/sv1k-rm2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">瑞典语</a>"}]},{"id":"segment-0039","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<em>La mayoría tienen versiones para hispanohablantes también</em>","zh":"<em>其中大多数也有面向西班牙语母语者的版本</em>"}},{"id":"segment-0040","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"While we're confident that our decks are the best options, we don't have options for ALL languages! But the Refold community can help you find a deck for your target language.","zh":"我们相信自己的牌组是最佳选择，但我们并未覆盖所有语言！不过，Refold 社区可以帮助你找到适合自己目标语言的牌组。"}},{"id":"when-to-move-beyond-pre-made-decks","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Move Beyond Pre-Made Decks","zh":"何时不再使用预制牌组"}},{"id":"segment-0042","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"As a beginner, pre-made frequency decks are ideal. They give you high-quality cards for the most common words. But once you're in the intermediate stages, making your own cards from your immersion (sentence mining) is more effective — the cards are easier to remember because they come from content you actually engaged with, and they're more relevant to what you're currently learning. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/sentence-mining\">Sentence Mining</a>","zh":"对于初学者来说，预制词频牌组是理想选择。它们能为最常见的单词提供高质量卡片。但进入中级阶段后，从自己的沉浸内容中制作卡片（句子挖掘）会更有效。这些卡片来自你真正接触过的内容，因此更容易记住，也与你当前所学的内容更相关。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/sentence-mining\">句子挖掘</a>"}},{"id":"research-and-reasoning","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Research and Reasoning","zh":"研究与依据"}},{"id":"segment-0044","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Spaced repetition as a learning technique is well-supported by memory research. Nakata (2015) studied its effects on second language vocabulary specifically and found significant benefits from spaced review compared to massed practice. Serfaty (2023) further explored how much relearning is necessary to retain vocabulary long-term.","zh":"作为一种学习方法，间隔重复得到了记忆研究的充分支持。Nakata（2015）专门研究了它对第二语言词汇学习的影响，发现与集中练习相比，间隔复习能带来显著益处。Serfaty（2023）则进一步探讨了要长期保留词汇，需要进行多少次重新学习。"}},{"id":"segment-0045","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The claim that vocabulary is the strongest predictor of reading comprehension comes from Nation (2001, 2006) and Stæhr (2008). Nation's work established the widely-cited coverage figures: the most common 1,000 words cover roughly 70% of text, and 2,000 words cover about 80%. These figures vary by language and corpus, but the pattern holds cross-linguistically. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/vocabulary-size\">Vocabulary Size</a>","zh":"“词汇量是阅读理解能力最强预测指标”这一观点源自 Nation（2001、2006）和 Stæhr（2008）的研究。Nation 的研究确立了广为引用的文本覆盖率数据：最常见的 1000 个单词大约覆盖文本的 70%，2000 个单词则覆盖约 80%。这些数据会因语言和语料库而异，但这一规律在不同语言中普遍成立。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/vocabulary-size\">词汇量</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0046","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The distinction between memorizing a word and acquiring it — the idea that Anki creates a dictionary entry but immersion fills it in — reflects the difference between deliberate and incidental vocabulary learning. Webb (2020) and others have shown that incidental acquisition through reading and listening is a major source of vocabulary growth, while deliberate study (like flashcards) is most effective as a way to prime the learner for that incidental acquisition. Nation (2001) argues that both deliberate and incidental learning have important roles, which is exactly the balance we recommend.","zh":"记住一个单词和真正习得它之间存在区别——也就是说，Anki 只是建立一个词典条目，而沉浸会逐渐充实这个条目。这反映了刻意词汇学习与附带词汇学习之间的差异。Webb（2020）等人的研究表明，通过阅读和听力进行的附带习得是词汇增长的主要来源，而像闪卡这样的刻意学习，最有效的作用是为学习者之后的附带习得做好准备。Nation（2001）认为，刻意学习和附带学习都发挥着重要作用，这正是我们所推荐的平衡方式。"}}],"cards":[]}}]
